    "content": "{\"id\": \"867ed0ec-e777-47ae-b4c4-f2e5d38d966f\", \"role\": \"assistant\", \"content\": [{\"text\": \"I couldn't find vol-0123456789abcdef0 in account 012345678901_1 in us-east-1. EC2 rejected the ID, and it isn't in the volume list for that region. I haven't changed anything.\\n\\nThe ID looks like a placeholder. It could also be a real volume in a different region or account.\\n\\nWhich of these should I do?\\n- **Different region or account:** tell me where the volume lives and I'll look there.\\n- **Different volume ID:** send me the right one.\\n\\nOnce I find the volume, I'll check its type and size before changing it. 10,000 IOPS only works on certain volume types:\\n- **gp3:** supports up to 500 IOPS per GiB, so it needs at least 20 GiB for 10,000 IOPS.\\n- **io1 and io2:** are also fine, within their IOPS-to-size ratios.\\n- **gp2:** can't be set directly, because its IOPS come from its size. It would have to be converted to gp3 or io2.\\n\\nThe change itself will go through your approval step. I'll treat your approval here as the go-ahead for this specific change, once I've confirmed the right volume.\", \"type\": \"text\"}], \"created_at\": null}",
